        "math_academy_id": "q-69922",
        "problem": "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=2t+1,\\,\\,\\,y=2t-1,\\,0\\le t\\le 5,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $3$ | $b$ | $7$ | $9$ | $11$ |\n| $y$ | $a$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $c$ | $9$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a-b-c.$",
        "worked_solution": "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=2(0)-1=0-1=-1.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=2$ into $x=2t+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=2(2)+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=4$ into $y=2t-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=2(4)-1=8-1=7.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na-b-c=-1-5-7=-13.\n$$",
